## **4. Known Limitations & Gaps**

### **TensorFlow.js**

| Limitation | Severity | Details |
|------------|----------|---------|
| **Browser Memory Constraints** | Medium | Limited by available browser RAM (typically 2-4GB) |
| **WebGL Dependency** | Medium | Some older devices lack WebGL 2.0 support |
| **Training Performance** | Medium | Training in browser ~10-100x slower than GPU on desktop |
| **Large Model Support** | Medium | Models >500MB challenging on mobile browsers |
| **Limited Quantization Control** | Low | Limited fine-grained quantization options compared to TensorFlow |
| **SIMD Support** | Low | WebAssembly SIMD adoption still in progress |

### **ONNX.js**

| Limitation | Severity | Details |
|------------|----------|---------|
| **No Training** | High | Inference-only (models must be trained elsewhere) |
| **Limited Model Zoo** | Medium | Smaller ecosystem of pre-trained models vs TFjs |
| **Custom Op Support** | Medium | Limited support for custom operations (depends on backend) |
| **Documentation Gaps** | Medium | Less comprehensive guides for specific frameworks |
| **Backend Maturity** | Medium | WebAssembly backend less mature than WebGL |
| **Memory Efficiency** | Low | Some inefficiencies vs TensorFlow.js in memory usage |

### **Brain.js**

| Limitation | Severity | Details |
|------------|----------|---------|
| **No GPU Support** | High | CPU-only (cannot leverage GPU acceleration) |
| **Limited Architecture Support** | High | Missing modern architectures (Transformers, Attention mechanisms) |
| **No Pre-trained Models** | High | Must train from scratch or implement custom loading |
| **Poor Scalability** | High | Not suitable for large datasets or complex models |
| **Community Maintenance** | Medium | Slower bug fixes and feature additions |
| **Type Safety** | Medium | Limited TypeScript definitions (added later) |
| **Data Processing** | High | Minimal pipeline support; manual preprocessing required |

