## **Library Selection Guidance**

### **Choose TensorFlow.js If:**
- You need comprehensive ML capabilities (training + inference)
- Pre-trained models will accelerate your development
- You require multi-platform deployment (web, mobile, Node.js)
- GPU acceleration is important
- You're building production-grade applications
- You need excellent documentation and community support

**Best Use Cases:** Computer vision apps, NLP tasks, real-time inference, transfer learning, full ML pipelines

### **Choose ONNX.js If:**
- You have models trained in PyTorch, TensorFlow, or other frameworks
- You need framework-agnostic model deployment
- Inference performance on existing models is your priority
- You're migrating from Python ML to JavaScript
- You need enterprise-grade stability

**Best Use Cases:** Model conversion pipelines, cross-framework deployment, inference-only applications

### **Choose Brain.js If:**
- You need a lightweight, zero-dependency solution (<50KB)
- Building simple neural networks or time-series models
- Browser bundle size is critical
- You don't need GPU acceleration
- Educational purposes or proof-of-concepts

**Best Use Cases:** Simple classification, basic neural networks, prototypes, lightweight browser apps

